extraction_notes: "SOURCE: Rifts World Book 8: Japan printed 102-105 (cache p103-p106, text layer, page_offset +1). The entry opens in the second column of printed 102 under Tsunami ''Borg; printed 103 is a full-page illustration with no text; the stat block runs through printed 104 and ends with item 7 on printed 105, where the Imperial Combat ''Borg follows. The soldier O.C.C. is printed 97-98, the shared bionics rules printed 96-97, the conversion age law printed 99. Printed 102, 104 and 105 and the soldier block were read off renders; every figure agrees with the text layer once the digit cipher is read (!D4xlO = 1D4x10, !D6xlOOO = 1D6x1000). || SHARED SKILLS: the five Republic cyborg classes (republic-cyborg-soldier, dragon-borg-wing-blade, dragon-borg-tsunami, dragon-borg-imperial-combat, dragon-borg-flame-cloud) restate ONE skill list, the Republic Cyborg Soldier O.C.C.''s (printed 97-98), and MUST BE CHANGED TOGETHER. Printed 101 says the dragon ''borgs have the same O.C.C. skills as the cyborg soldier unless a police officer or mercenary. Identical in all five: O.C.C., related and secondary skills, hand to hand, XP table, starting money, occ_group and men_of_arms, the M.E. requirement, the human-only race restriction and the standard military issue. What differs is the body: the four dragon ''borgs are one class per body (mdc_base, fixed P.S./P.P./Spd, unconditional combat bonuses, weapons and features), following the Free Quebec cyborgs (fq-cyborg-*, BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F31). || XP: the Dragon Borg, Japanese Borg column on the Experience Point Tables page (cache p217, printed folio 216), fourth column, bottom block, read off a render: 0 / 2,176 / 4,301 / 8,401 / 17,501 / 24,601 / 36,701 / 44,801 / 57,901 / 94,001 / 130,001 / 190,001 / 240,001 / 280,001 / 330,001. || GROUP: men-of-arms with men_of_arms: true in all five Republic cyborg classes, following fq-cyborg-soldier and cs-cyborg-strike-trooper; the book files the Republic''s cyborgs with no group heading. The soldier states no pool, so the line picks its S.D.C. roll; a dragon ''borg states mdc_base, and the line is kept so the five agree. || BODY: mdc_base is the main body''s 320 only. The book prints the body''s physical attributes as P.S. 26, P.P. 23, Spd 176, stored as fixed attribute_dice following plains-borg and this book''s ninja-borg; the P.P. 23 bonus of +4 strike, parry and dodge the book prints is what the app derives from that P.P. and is not added again. The combat bonuses (+2 initiative, +2 parry, +1 dodge, +2 pull punch, +1 roll, +2 vs horror factor) and the +1 attack (tail) are the body''s and apply always, so they are stored. The Free Quebec chassis keep their M.D.C. by location and weapons in a `vehicles` row; no vehicles row exists for the dragon ''borgs, so the body''s locations, weapons, movement and features are special_abilities here. The wings'' +10% to jet pack piloting, and -20% with a wing lost, are the body''s and are prose in the Movement ability, not folded into the shared Jet Packs figure. || SKILLS: catalog base plus printed bonus: Mathematics: Basic 45+10, Radio: Basic 45+10, Computer Operation 40+10, Jet Packs 42+20 (printed Pilot Jet Pack), Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+10, Find Contraband 26+10 (printed Find Contraband, Weapons & Cybernetics), Land Navigation 36+10, Climbing 40+10, Swimming 50+10. Literacy: Japanese at 98% stored as Literacy: Native Language at the book''s 98, fixed; Language: Japanese 98% as Language: Native Tongue; one language of choice (+15%) as a Language: Other pick. W.P. Heavy Energy Weapons is W.P. Heavy M.D. Weapons, as fq-cyborg-soldier stores it. Hand to Hand: Basic Martial Arts/Judo is this book''s row; the upgrade prices (Aikido or Karate one pick, Jujitsu two) are the hand_to_hand block. The Jet Packs figure is the soldier''s +20% in all five; a body''s own bonus to jet pack piloting stays in that body''s prose. || RELATED: five plus one at levels 4, 8 and 12. SECONDARY: none at level one; two each at levels 2, 5, 8 and 13, as printed (the FQ soldier''s ninth-level slot is 8 here), from the related list excluding those marked None and without the bonuses. || NOT STORED: those assigned to demolitions automatically get Demolitions Disposal and Demolitions (both +10%) as extra skills (printed 105); an assignment, so prose here. || EQUIPMENT: the standard military issue (printed 98), identical in all five Republic cyborg classes: the energy rifle is unspecified, so it is a choice of this book''s ArmaTech and H-Brand energy rifles (the stun rifle and the underwater rifle left out); four extra E-clips are the rifle E-clip row; four grenades are a choice of this book''s grenades excluding the armor dissolver, as printed (four of one kind; a mix is the GM''s call); distancing binoculars are infrared-distancing-binoculars; the backpack is pr-1-standard-backpack, this book''s standard pack. The body-styling ammunition, maintenance and repairs are not items, and the jet pack, hover vehicle and extra weapons available upon assignment are not starting kit. The Tsunami adds the concealed leg compartment kit (printed 104); the laser rod option has no catalog row and is not stubbed. The 3D6x1000 credit anime consultant fee (printed 102) is an in-play reward, not starting money. || MONEY: monthly salary 2,000 credits (officers of 9th level and up 3,500 to 5,000; police ''borgs 800 more than an unaugmented officer); starting_money holds the 1D6x1000 the book gives as a first-level character''s savings. Room, board, clothing and medical care are provided. The text layer ciphers the savings as !D6xlOOO. || PRINTED ODDITIES, stored as printed or not stored: the tail reach is printed 6 feet (3.6 m), and 6 feet is 1.8 m; the jet pack''s low speed is printed 80 mph/108 kph; the lore mentions vibro-claws on the hands and feet that the weapon systems never give damage for."
---

## Lore

The Tsunami is the second largest dragon ''borg the Republic produces, a
heavy combat model built for the military and the police. The big city police
departments keep a small detachment of them to deal with Oni, supernatural
menaces and the odd renegade or criminal ''borg, and even fully bionic humanoid
''borgs respect and fear them. In the military they fight beside the infantry or
support power armor troops on every kind of mission, from search and destroy to
scouting and sabotage. Their draconic look alone sometimes frightens
superstitious peasants and even lesser demons.

A built-in jet pack gives the Tsunami limited flight, but it is a ground
fighter at heart and nowhere near as fast or agile in the air as flying power
armor. Its arsenal runs from an arm-mounted mini-gun and laser eyes to a pair of
mini-missiles on the back and vibro-claws on the hands and feet.

The inhuman body and the violence of the job wear on some of those who wear it,
but most Tsunami ''borgs serve with distinction. Their deeds fill patriotic
posters, films and manga, above all the long-running animated serial
"Demon-Hunter Tsunami", and a ''borg with a true heroic story to tell may be paid
a consulting fee to see it animated.

## GM Notes

Standard military issue for cyborg soldiers is all the ammunition and equipment
for the body''s weapon systems, an energy rifle of choice, four extra E-clips,
four grenades (no armor dissolvers unless the assignment calls for them),
distancing binoculars, a utility belt, a backpack, a walkie-talkie for back-up,
and regular maintenance and repairs. Available on assignment: a jet pack, a
hover vehicle or other transport, additional weapons and equipment. The
character has medium security clearance to most military bases, hospitals and
facilities, and all basic needs are provided: a private room in a four-soldier
dormitory barracks, or off-base housing at his own expense. Officers of 9th
level and higher are paid 3,500 to 5,000 credits a month, and police ''borgs 800
credits a month more than an ordinary officer. Rank runs from private to
general.

A Tsunami assigned to demolitions automatically gets Demolitions and
Demolitions Disposal (both +10%) as extra skills. A ''borg whose true exploits
are adapted for anime may be paid a 3D6x1000 credit consultant fee.

When a ''borg leaves service (printed 98) he may keep basic bionics and live as
a registered citizen with external weapons removed, keep most systems after a
long or heroic career if he moves to authorized security or police work or
leaves the Republic as a mercenary, or undergo retro-conversion to bio-systems
or a clone body. A full conversion ''borg with good maintenance may stay active
for 300 years or more.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dragon-borg-tsunami');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dragon-borg-tsunami';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-dragon-borg-tsunami-class.sql');
